WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.390
My first sock here is my sclera.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.320
Second layer, the uvea, which is made of the choroid,

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.720
the iris and the ciliary bodies.

4
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:15.240
I remove that, and then I'm left with the retina, which is made first of two main

5
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.180
large layers, the outer retina and the inner retina.

6
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.490
This is where the detachment occurs, this is where we have the moment when we have

7
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.460
the primitive optic cup that comes like this, making a juxta connection.

8
00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:31.597
of acrine, with the superficial epiblast that will thicken,

9
00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:35.427
that will create the outer optic placode, which is as if held,

10
00:00:35.427 --> 00:00:36.907
and around it, it grows.

11
00:00:36.907 --> 00:00:39.147
This gives this primitive depression.

12
00:00:39.757 --> 00:00:42.167
Then, it will be integrated like this.

13
00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:46.787
We have the meeting of this retina that comes to surround itself and that's where it

14
00:00:46.787 --> 00:00:49.517
will create what we call the outer retina and the inner

15
00:00:49.857 --> 00:00:54.737
retina. This is where you have retinal detachment. Some people have a detachment.

16
00:00:56.114 --> 00:00:57.034
of the retina.

17
00:00:57.034 --> 00:00:58.754
You've already heard about that.

18
00:00:58.754 --> 00:01:00.504
That's where it happens, actually.

19
00:01:00.504 --> 00:01:04.674
And the retina, if you look, that's really brain, ventricular tissue.

